      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got the following trace:\n\u003e ERR btadapterd[17707]: bluetooth:  audio_hal_interface/a2dp_encoding_host.cc:133 - StartRequest: StartRequest: call state is busy\n\nSee [a2dp_encoding_host.cc](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2843515/comment/e37bc2fc_e64d6f3d/) and [btif_hf.cc](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/aosp/packages/modules/Bluetooth/local/system/btif/src/btif_hf.cc;drc\u003d1a95b7c28cb8f45f4e4a7f970f9f908eef5f4525;l\u003d802)\n\nOn WebHID disconnection, there should be no more HID call else it will prevents A2DP to start.\nSo, it seems to me that this is mandatory to keep lower HF C++ layer in sink with the Rust layer.",
      "parentUuid": "e37bc2fc_e64d6f3d",
